---
title: "Regression Analysis"
format:
  html:
    code-copy: true
    theme: cosmo
    toc: true
    lightbox: auto
---

Regression models describe and quantify the relationship between an outcome and one or more predictors. This module builds up in tiers — start with a single predictor, then add predictors, then move on to diagnostics and logistic regression.

::: {.content-visible when-profile="regression"}

## Full-day workshop: Theory of Regression Analysis

This page is a quick tour. For the full-day, thesis-level treatment — six slide decks, six fill-in-the-blank R labs and a self-check quiz after every session — use the **Regression Workshop** menu above. Everything runs on one simulated adult NCD survey (n = 600, 20 villages).

| Session | Topics | Deck | Lab |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 · Foundations | What regression is · model-selection flowchart | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s1_foundations.qmd) | `lab1_explore.R` |
| 2 · Simple linear regression | Slope in units · CI vs PI · R² · centering | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s2_simple_regression.qmd) | `lab2_simple.R` |
| 3 · Inference & multiple regression | Confounding · dummy coding · model building | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s3_multiple_regression.qmd) | `lab3_multiple.R` |
| 4 · Assumptions | LINE + collinearity, with fixes | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s4_assumptions.qmd) | `lab4_assumptions.R` |
| 5 · Logistic regression | Odds · likelihood · ROC · OR vs PR | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s5_logistic_regression.qmd) | `lab5_logistic.R` |
| 6 · Interpreting & reporting | Writing results · pitfalls · what next | [Slides](../regression-workshop/s6_reporting.qmd) | `lab6_reporting.R` |

Also: the [interpretation cheat sheet](../regression-workshop/cheatsheet.qmd), the [dataset](../data/ncd_survey.csv) and the [labs and data-simulation script](../downloads.qmd).

:::

## Simple Linear Regression


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
library(tidyverse)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}

```
